NullMoth NVIDIA Metal driver — third-party components

The licence texts below ship in the package's licenses/ folder and are installed to /Library/NullMoth/licenses.

translator/  Based on metal2vulkan, Copyright (C) Anees Iqbal
             https://github.com/steelbrain/metal2vulkan
             Licensed under the GNU Lesser General Public License v3.0 or later
             (translator/LICENSE, translator/COPYING). Modifications by NullMoth Systems
             are released under the same licence.

kexts/       Builds against NVIDIA's open GPU kernel modules 620.70.06, MIT (with GPL-2.0 alternatives
             where noted), https://github.com/NVIDIA/open-gpu-kernel-modules
             (licenses/NVIDIA-open-gpu-kernel-modules-COPYING.txt).

NVK          Vulkan driver from Mesa, MIT (licenses/Mesa-license.rst). NullMoth's changes ship as patches.

GSP firmware gsp_tu10x.bin, gsp_ga10x.bin and the matching ucode images from NVIDIA's 620.70.06 driver,
             redistributed unmodified under NVIDIA's licence (licenses/NVIDIA-firmware-LICENCE.txt), the same
             terms under which linux-firmware redistributes these images.

kexts/NMIntelFB  Panel brightness follows the method of WhateverXe's panel PWM (XELP::PanelPWM) by b00t0x,
             https://github.com/b00t0x/WhateverXe, BSD-3-Clause, Copyright (c) 2018 vit9696
             (licenses/WhateverXe-LICENSE.txt). Register layout from Linux i915/xe display headers, MIT.
             No Apple driver code is used or shipped.

NMXAudio     The HD Audio controller and codec layers are FreeBSD's snd_hda (sys/dev/sound/pci/hda: hdac.c,
             hdaa.c, hdacc.c, hdaa_patches.c), BSD-2-Clause (licenses/FreeBSD-snd_hda-LICENSE.txt).
             Installed on macOS 26 only, where macOS has no HD Audio driver.

vendor/nvenc  Video encoders and decoders for NVIDIA's NVENC and NVDEC engines, offered to apps through VideoToolbox
             (libnvencvt.dylib). mickys/nvenc, https://github.com/mickys/nvenc, MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 mickys
             (licenses/mickys-nvenc-LICENSE.txt). The source is imported unchanged apart from one added
             function; vendor/nvenc/SOURCE lists the commit and the change. Builds against NVIDIA's MIT-licensed
             open-gpu-kernel-modules and open-gpu-doc headers and Apple's decoder interface as published in WebKit (BSD).

translator/  The Rust crates linked into the translator (bitflags, itoa, libc, memchr, serde, syn and others, all MIT and/or
             Apache-2.0, one Unlicense-or-MIT) keep their licences: licenses/translator-rust-crates.txt has each licence text.

dlss/        dlss/zstd is the Zstandard 1.5.6 reference decoder, BSD-3-Clause (licenses/zstd-LICENSE.txt); dlss/blake3 is BLAKE3 1.8.2 as
             vendored by Mesa, used under CC0 1.0 (licenses/BLAKE3-LICENSE-CC0.txt). The package carries no NVIDIA DLSS code: NVIDIA's
             DLSS runtimes, NGX core and nvJitLink are downloaded by the user's Mac from NVIDIA's public sources, checked against
             pinned hashes, and stay under NVIDIA's licences (package/dlss_fetch.sh).

air-runtime  LLVM (Apache-2.0 with LLVM exceptions) and Zstandard (BSD-3-Clause); their licence texts are in
             NVMTLDriver.bundle/Contents/Resources/air-runtime.

kexts/NVRMFB EDID override files and the opt-in smaller boot rasters follow an idea by mickys
             (https://github.com/mickys/nvidia-macos-driver, commit 9c023cd), proposed for this project in
             pull request 468 by GeekAudio. The implementation here is written independently.

kexts/NVRM   BAR1 placement is clipped to the range IOKit can describe and the aperture list is built before any
             PCI write (nvrm_bar_limits.h, placeLargeBar1). Community contribution: pull requests #431 (GeekAudio)
             and #473 (Giraffe12311), based on the bar-preflight experiment by yuanjing-hash.

Community ideas  The shared family-VRAM import cache and the browser surface-publication default follow ideas first
             published by mickys (https://github.com/mickys/nvidia-macos-driver, PolyForm Noncommercial 1.0.0) and
             proposed to this project by GeekAudio in pull requests 463 and 481. The code here is NullMoth's own.
